from pathlib import Path

p = Path('DEVELOPMENT_HANDOFF.md')
s = p.read_text()
title = '### 2026-09-10 — Smooth the 420ms window transition'
start = s.index(title)
next_start = s.find('\n### ', start + len(title))
if next_start < 0:
    next_start = len(s)
block = s[start:next_start]
if '**Status: IN PROGRESS**' not in block:
    raise SystemExit('target entry is not IN PROGRESS')
block = block.replace('**Status: IN PROGRESS**', '**Status: COMPLETED**', 1)
summary = '''\n#### Completion summary\n\n- **Result:** COMPLETED. The 420ms rightward screen transition no longer uses Chrome's full-page root View Transition snapshot path that was producing a visible mid-swipe hitch on heavier destinations. Navigation now keeps the outgoing screen fixed and opaque while the destination is activated and allowed to lay out underneath, then animates only that outgoing screen with transform and opacity. This moves expensive destination work ahead of visible motion instead of allowing it to interrupt the middle of the glide.\n- **Root cause / iteration:** The original 420ms transition combined four eased keyframe segments, blur from 0px to 11px, and full-root View Transition snapshot capture. CSS-only candidate runs `34557077950`, `34557134059`, and `34557217844` were deliberately rejected before product commit. Removing blur/intermediate keyframes improved the animation itself, but repeated cadence profiling still showed reproducible 66.7ms stalls specifically when entering Level Select. That isolated the remaining hitch to root snapshot capture/paint rather than the easing curve.\n- **Implementation:** `game400-a.js` now provides a contract-compatible manual transition controller with `ready`, `finished`, and `skipTransition()` promises/methods. It swaps the destination underneath the fixed outgoing screen, waits two animation frames for layout/paint preparation, then animates the outgoing screen to the right over a nominal 420ms using only `transform` and `opacity` with `cubic-bezier(.22,.61,.36,1)`. `style400-ui.css` removes the old `::view-transition-*`/blur keyframes and adds the lightweight `.screen-transition-outgoing` overlay treatment. Existing screen-swipe SFX, sequencing that waits on `activeScreenTransition.finished`, reduced-motion immediate swaps, and rapid-navigation cancellation are preserved.\n- **Product / cleanup commits:** Accepted product commit `0c2cbc67f626b6063f10db2dbed32283834792c2` (`Eliminate screen transition stutter`) changed only `game400-a.js` and `style400-ui.css`. Temporary validation helpers self-removed in clean-state commit `a506dc2c1caefd63c9e9ea1796cb3f5dc10ef47d` (`Remove smooth transition validator`).\n- **Acceptance:** GitHub Actions run `34557738451`, job `103133898968`, completed successfully and printed `SMOOTH_WINDOW_TRANSITION_ACCEPTED`. It exercised Level Select twice, Home, Story, Game, reduced motion, and rapid navigation. All transitions ended with exactly one active screen and no leftover outgoing overlay, with no page errors or horizontal overflow.\n- **Cadence evidence:** The first cold Level Select sample prepared for 34.2ms, then completed visible motion without the old 66.7ms mid-transition stall; its largest observed motion-frame gap was 50.1ms. The second Level Select entry was clean at a 16.8ms maximum gap and 16.67ms average cadence. Home, Story, and Game steady-state samples also stayed at approximately 16.7ms maximum/average frame cadence. Destination preparation was consistently about 31–34ms and happened before visible motion.\n- **Scope protection:** Hash verification confirmed `game400-b.js`, `sfx400.js`, `music400.js`, `index.html`, `style400-board-surfaces.css`, `style400-atlas-progression.css`, story/cinematic sources, and all eight `campaign400-*.js` files were unchanged. Board visuals and audio tuning from the previous task were not modified.\n- **Artifact / visual review:** Acceptance artifact `smooth-window-transition-renders`, artifact ID `10183201320`, SHA-256 `54bd106286a9571e20a994deb81a7bbcf26a328cfc4d245b747e5ce7a922eb00`, contains seven sampled transition frames plus `report.json`. Manual review found no duplicate screen, stray overlay, partial destination paint, or flash. The cadence measurements are the primary smoothness signal because screenshot capture itself cannot reliably sample compositor motion at exact frame times.\n- **Deployment / hygiene:** GitHub Pages run `34557818661` successfully deployed clean accepted state `a506dc2c1caefd63c9e9ea1796cb3f5dc10ef47d`. Before this closeout helper was created, `.github/workflows` contained only `validate-repository-access-guard.yml`. This closeout helper self-removes after committing the journal update.\n- **Remaining risk / next action:** No known blocker remains. The first cold Level Select navigation can still spend roughly 30–35ms preparing the complex destination before the glide begins, but that work is now hidden behind the fully opaque outgoing screen rather than appearing as a mid-animation freeze. Device testing on the user's Android build remains the best final subjective check for feel.\n'''
if '#### Completion summary' in block:
    raise SystemExit('completion summary already present')
block = block.rstrip() + '\n' + summary + '\n'
s = s[:start] + block + s[next_start:]
p.write_text(s)
print('SMOOTH_TRANSITION_HANDOFF_CLOSED')
